{"content":[{"c":["PISHON"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["First of four divisions of the river that flowed out of the Garden of Eden (",{"href":"?bref=Gen.2.11","r":"Gen.2.11","rawR":"Gen.2.11","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Gen.2.11","value":"Gen.2.11"}],"t":"ref","v":"Gn 2:11"},"). Suggestions for its identity include the Rion, the Indus, the Ganges, a canal connecting the Tigris and Euphrates, and a symbol of the Milky Way. No consensus exists on Pishon’s identity."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"Pishon","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Gn 2:11","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Gen.2.11","rawQueryValue":"Gen.2.11","sourceRefExact":"Gen.2.11"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"6dda99ffebcc28651e5f6ecb4aae356869676094bfe3d8b70f7e157ea1d4d8d5","sourceItemName":"Pishon","sourceItemOrder":202,"sourceMember":"Articles/P.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"Pishon","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Pishon","title":"Pishon","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}